From: Angel Martinez <110217098+anmartinez1256@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:01:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/43] Metal diamond engine: Drude/Lorentz materials and
 conducting sheets on the GPU (snapshot cg22)

Engine_Ext_LorentzMaterial (exactly that class: Drude/Lorentz materials and the
conducting sheets, which are an order-2 Lorentz extension with voltage ADEs) runs
per tile on the GPU: the Pre stage (ADE and Lorentz term from the field before the
update) shares the Mur Pre stage, before the UPML Pre stage that writes the field;
Apply (field -= ADE, the orders one after the other) runs in the extension-order
Apply list with Mur and RLC in the E step and before the current excitation in the
H step. The arithmetic follows clang's contraction of the CPU code (Lor += v_Lor*ADE
one fmadd; ADE *= v_int and ADE += v_ext*(f - Lor) as two statements). A position
repeated within one order makes Apply run on one thread in list order.

All six benchmark models now run on the GPU; the GCPW line (conducting sheets, Mur,
lumped port): port probes and S-parameters bit-identical to the multithreaded engine
with OPENEMS_FTZ=1. emsKit diamond_check.sh 48 of 48 (new: conducting sheets on a Mur
box; PML + Mur + lumped RLC + two Drude/Lorentz blocks with eps and mue ADEs, with and
without the Lorentz pole, + conducting sheets). The CPU code changes only by friend
declarations.

